{"id":"faults-behind-in-front","rev":2,"lang":"en","status":"published","review_flag":null,"disclaimer":null,"title":"Behind, in front, over, under, chipped","summary":"What “behind”, “in front”, “over”, “under” and “chipped” mean, what usually causes each miss, and how a chipped target is scored.","body":[{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-p1","t":"p","html":"Each miss has a direction. A coach watching from behind the shooter usually says first where the shot went compared with the clay, and only then why.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"dg-miss-directions","t":"diagram","html":"<figure class=\"dg\" aria-labelledby=\"dg-miss-directions\"><p class=\"dg-h\" id=\"dg-miss-directions\">Where the shot went: behind, in front, over, under</p><svg class=\"dg-svg\" viewBox=\"40 10 640 372\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"dg-miss-directions\" focusable=\"false\"><path class=\"dg-fly\" d=\"M60 190 H592\"/><path class=\"dg-flyh\" d=\"M592 182 l14 8 -14 8z\"/>\n<circle class=\"dg-pat\" cx=\"200\" cy=\"190\" r=\"52\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"210.0\" cy=\"190.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"187.5\" cy=\"201.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"202.1\" cy=\"166.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"218.9\" cy=\"214.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"162.6\" cy=\"183.4\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"238.0\" cy=\"165.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"196.9\" cy=\"201.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"191.2\" cy=\"173.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"224.4\" cy=\"198.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"169.5\" cy=\"202.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"217.0\" cy=\"153.8\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"214.0\" cy=\"234.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"187.9\" cy=\"183.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"220.5\" cy=\"185.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"183.9\" cy=\"212.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"195.5\" cy=\"155.3\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"232.1\" cy=\"217.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"151.0\" cy=\"192.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"211.3\" cy=\"178.7\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"198.9\" cy=\"213.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"180.8\" cy=\"167.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"236.7\" cy=\"195.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-pat\" cx=\"460\" cy=\"190\" r=\"52\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"470.0\" cy=\"190.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"447.5\" cy=\"201.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"462.1\" cy=\"166.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"478.9\" cy=\"214.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"422.6\" cy=\"183.4\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"498.0\" cy=\"165.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"456.9\" cy=\"201.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"451.2\" cy=\"173.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"484.4\" cy=\"198.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"429.5\" cy=\"202.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"477.0\" cy=\"153.8\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"474.0\" cy=\"234.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"447.9\" cy=\"183.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"480.5\" cy=\"185.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"443.9\" cy=\"212.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"455.5\" cy=\"155.3\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"492.1\" cy=\"217.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"411.0\" cy=\"192.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"471.3\" cy=\"178.7\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"458.9\" cy=\"213.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"440.8\" cy=\"167.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"496.7\" cy=\"195.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-pat\" cx=\"330\" cy=\"74\" r=\"52\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"340.0\" cy=\"74.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"317.5\" cy=\"85.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"332.1\" cy=\"50.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"348.9\" cy=\"98.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"292.6\" cy=\"67.4\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"368.0\" cy=\"49.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"326.9\" cy=\"85.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"321.2\" cy=\"57.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"354.4\" cy=\"82.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"299.5\" cy=\"86.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"347.0\" cy=\"37.8\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"344.0\" cy=\"118.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"317.9\" cy=\"67.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"350.5\" cy=\"69.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"313.9\" cy=\"96.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"325.5\" cy=\"39.3\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"362.1\" cy=\"101.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"281.0\" cy=\"76.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"341.3\" cy=\"62.7\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"328.9\" cy=\"97.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"310.8\" cy=\"51.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"366.7\" cy=\"79.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-pat\" cx=\"330\" cy=\"306\" r=\"52\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"340.0\" cy=\"306.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"317.5\" cy=\"317.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"332.1\" cy=\"282.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"348.9\" cy=\"330.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"292.6\" cy=\"299.4\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"368.0\" cy=\"281.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"326.9\" cy=\"317.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"321.2\" cy=\"289.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"354.4\" cy=\"314.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"299.5\" cy=\"318.6\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"347.0\" cy=\"269.8\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"344.0\" cy=\"350.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"317.9\" cy=\"299.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"350.5\" cy=\"301.5\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"313.9\" cy=\"328.9\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"325.5\" cy=\"271.3\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"362.1\" cy=\"333.1\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"281.0\" cy=\"308.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"341.3\" cy=\"294.7\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"328.9\" cy=\"329.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"310.8\" cy=\"283.0\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle class=\"dg-sh\" cx=\"366.7\" cy=\"311.0\" r=\"2.2\"/>\n<ellipse class=\"dg-tg\" cx=\"330\" cy=\"190\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"6\"/>\n<rect class=\"dg-inset\" x=\"540\" y=\"262\" width=\"124\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\"/><circle class=\"dg-pat\" cx=\"585\" cy=\"328\" r=\"34\"/><ellipse class=\"dg-tg\" cx=\"612\" cy=\"298\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"5\"/><path class=\"dg-tg\" d=\"M624 290 l8 -6 2 5z\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"160\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">1</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"500\" cy=\"160\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"500\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">2</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"40\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">3</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"288\" cy=\"330\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"288\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">4</text></g><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"628\" cy=\"290\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"628\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">5</text></g></svg><ol class=\"dg-leg\"><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">1</b>Behind: not enough lead, or the gun slowed down</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">2</b>In front: too much lead</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">3</b>Over: often the head came off the stock</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">4</b>Under: the target was still climbing</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">5</b>Chipped: caught by the edge of the pattern; a visible piece is a hit</li></ol><figcaption>The target flies to the right. Each circle is the pattern, the cloud of shot. Behind is the side the target came from.</figcaption></figure>","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-p2","t":"p","html":"Behind means the shot passed behind a moving target: not enough lead, or a gun that slowed down. It is a very common miss on crossers. In front is the opposite: too much lead, often after the shooter over-corrected. Many coaches like a miss in front: it shows the gun kept moving.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-p3","t":"p","html":"Over (also 'high', 'over the top') and under ('low') describe the vertical miss. Over is common on dropping targets, rabbits and incomers, and is often linked to the head coming off the stock. Under is typical on rising targets that are still climbing at the shot.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-p4","t":"p","html":"Chipped means only a small piece came off. For the coach it is half praise, half correction: the clay was caught by the edge of the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/pattern/\">pattern</a>, the cloud of shot. For the referee it is a hit, as long as the piece is visible. Watch out for one rule detail. A clay that breaks, even if it turns wholly or partly to dust, is a hit in both disciplines. A clay that flies on in one piece and gives off only a puff of dust or smoke, with no visible piece, is a miss (zero). In coach slang 'smoked it' means a perfect, centred hit that turns the clay to dust, and 'dusted it' is heard in both senses, so ask when unsure.","disc":"both","rule_ref":null},{"k":"technique-follow-through-and-mistakes-p5","t":"tip","html":"Many of these misses are easy to see from outside. A coach standing behind you sees where the shot went and what your head, hands and feet did. On your own you may fix the wrong thing: a shot behind from a stopped gun is not cured by more lead.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null}],"notes":[{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-n1","for":"interpreter","html":"Pass the direction on at once: the shooter is already preparing for the next target."},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-p5","for":"interpreter","html":"Keep the coach's order: direction, cause, fix. If the coach says 'behind, you stopped', the cause matters more: a shooter who hears only 'behind' will add lead, which does not cure a stopped gun."}],"phrases":[{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-ph1","speaker":"coach","en":"Behind, give it more.","meaning":"The shot passed behind the clay; increase the lead.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-ph2","speaker":"coach","en":"Just over the top, it was already dropping.","meaning":"The shot went above because the clay was falling; shoot lower and in front.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-ph3","speaker":"coach","en":"In front this time, good, now a touch less.","meaning":"Too much lead, but the gun was moving; reduce the lead slightly.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-ph4","speaker":"coach","en":"You just chipped it, a little more in front.","meaning":"Hit on the edge of the pattern; a bit more lead centres it.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-ph5","speaker":"coach","en":"Smoked it! Same again.","meaning":"A perfect centred hit (slang, not the rules' 'smoke'); repeat exactly.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-ph6","speaker":"coach","en":"Behind, but you stopped, so don't just add lead.","meaning":"The cause is a stopped gun; more lead alone will not help.","say":null,"audio":1}],"key_points":[{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-kp1","html":"The coach names the direction first: behind, in front, over, under.","checklist":false},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-kp2","html":"Behind = too little lead or a slowing gun; in front = too much lead.","checklist":false},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-kp3","html":"A visible chip, or a clay turned to dust, is a hit; an intact clay giving off only dust or smoke is a zero.","checklist":false},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-kp4","html":"'Smoked it' is coach praise, not the 'smoke' of the rules: do not mix them up.","checklist":false},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-kp5","html":"Fix the cause, not only the direction: more lead does not cure a stopped gun.","checklist":false}],"did_you_know":{"k":"technique-follow-through-and-mistakes-dyk","html":"A coach often stands slightly behind and to one side of the shooter. From there it is easier to see the shot’s trail in the air and where it passed the target."},"quiz":[{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-q1","q":"The coach calls: 'Behind, you stopped!' What matters most for the next shot?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"The cause: the gun stopped"},{"k":"b","text":"Only the direction 'behind'"},{"k":"c","text":"Nothing: you saw the miss yourself"},{"k":"d","text":"A request to add a lot more lead"}],"correct":"a","explain":"Adding lead does not cure a stopped gun; the cause is what the shooter has to fix."},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-q2","q":"A small but clearly visible piece breaks off the clay. The coach says 'just chipped it'. How does the referee score it?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"Lost, because most of the clay flew on"},{"k":"b","text":"No Bird"},{"k":"c","text":"One (hit)"},{"k":"d","text":"Hit only if the coach agrees"}],"correct":"c","explain":"At least one visible piece makes the target a hit in both Sporting™ and Compak® Sporting; the referee decides alone.","rule_ref":"sporting:ch6-target-one","disc":"both"},{"k":"faults-behind-in-front-q3","q":"After a hit the coach shouts 'Smoked it!'. What does he mean?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"Only dust came off, so it is lost"},{"k":"b","text":"A perfect, centred hit"},{"k":"c","text":"It was a flash target"},{"k":"d","text":"The shooter should change cartridges"}],"correct":"b","explain":"In coach slang 'smoked it' is praise for a clay turned to dust, and the rules count that as a hit too. Only an intact clay that gives off a puff of dust or smoke, with no visible piece, is a zero."}],"terms":[{"id":"lead","en":"Lead","local":"","label":"Lead","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/lead/"},{"id":"crosser","en":"Crosser","local":"","label":"Crosser","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/crosser/"},{"id":"dropping-target","en":"Dropping target","local":"","label":"Dropping target","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/dropping-target/"},{"id":"visible-piece","en":"Visible piece","local":"","label":"Visible piece","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/visible-piece/"},{"id":"one","en":"One","local":"","label":"One","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/one/"},{"id":"zero","en":"Zero","local":"","label":"Zero","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/zero/"},{"id":"miss-behind","en":"Behind","local":"","label":"Behind","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/miss-behind/"},{"id":"miss-in-front","en":"In front","local":"","label":"In front","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/miss-in-front/"},{"id":"miss-over","en":"Over","local":"","label":"Over","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/miss-over/"},{"id":"miss-under","en":"Under","local":"","label":"Under","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/miss-under/"},{"id":"chip","en":"Chip","local":"","label":"Chip","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/chip/"},{"id":"smoked-it","en":"Smoked it","local":"","label":"Smoked it","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/smoked-it/"},{"id":"pattern","en":"Pattern","local":"","label":"Pattern","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/pattern/"}],"rule_refs":[{"book":"sporting","id":"ch6-target-one","label":"Chapter 6 · When a target is scored 'one' (hit)","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/sporting/target-refereeing/#ch6-target-one"},{"book":"sporting","id":"ch6-target-zero","label":"Chapter 6 · When a target is scored 'zero' (lost)","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/sporting/target-refereeing/#ch6-target-zero"},{"book":"compak","id":"ch20-one","label":"Chapter 20 · When a target is a hit (ONE)","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/compak/judging-targets/#ch20-one"},{"book":"compak","id":"ch20-zero","label":"Chapter 20 · When a target is a miss (ZERO)","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/compak/judging-targets/#ch20-zero"}],"sources":[{"title":"FITASC — rules of Parcours de Chasse – Sporting™ and Compak® Sporting","url":"https://www.fitasc.com/disciplines-sportives/reglements-sportifs","fitasc":true}],"evidence":[],"more_in_en":0}
